    engine 1.0.3: input-parity conformance (zone_memory 5->3)
    
    Root cause of the 2026-06-23 3C parity break (and the May 23/27 divergences):
    the engine hardcoded zone_memory=5 for 5m exec while the deployed Pine runs
    zoneMemory=3 (input default, operator-verified on both charts). Logic/bands/EMAs
    are line-identical; the single constant forked hadPrimeEp/activeZone state.
    
    - Fix: Cell.zone_memory -> 3 (all mandates). No signal-logic change.
    - Input-parity fixtures (test_i_input_parity.py + pine_defaults_manifest.yaml):
      every signal constant (both configs) + zone_memory (all mandates) asserted vs
      the .pine defaults; behavioral pins at zone_memory=3 (no PRIME May 23 16:20,
      no grade-C May 27 12:45, no CONFIRMs Jun 23 17:00/17:45/20:45).
    - Journal: mem=5 parity + naiad_v0 dryrun journals archived to
      journal_mem5_archive/ (zoneMemory-5 v12 seed); parity journal regenerated at
      mem=3 (run_id 1869ff70, engine 1.0.3); I3 diff vs validated shadow = ZERO.
    - Case windows regenerated; sign-off note states verified inputs.
    - ENGINE_VERSION 1.0.2 -> 1.0.3; CHANGELOG + LEDGER entries.
    - Suite 47 passed / 1 skipped (was 40): +8 input-parity fixtures; F8b dryrun
      scan flips pass->skip (dryrun journal archived; skipif-guarded, unmodified).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

